  <!--
  The trimmed structures are declared with pragma pack(2), so a one byte field followed by a wider
  one is padded to an even offset. The specification lists only the fields, leaving those gaps
  visible as jumps in its offset column; they are transcribed here as explicit Reserved fields
  named for the offset they occupy, because without them every following field would decode one
  byte early.

  Transaction Code is carried by the framing in Nse.NnfTrimmed.Tcp.v1.0.Source.xml and is not
  repeated in the message fields, so each message begins at offset two.
  -->

